Why would you have to drop it and then loot?  Just apply it.

Once I have them, I always keep 1 wand of fire (or lightning if I
don't have fire) in main inventory, and one teleport, and one digging,
and one death.

Note that /fire and /lightning are _not_ primarily for attacking in
Vanilla: fire/lightning will burn permanent Elbereth, which saves you
from just about everything aside from A, @, and minotaurs (unless you
blind them (by zapping /lightning at them for example) or they're
summoners that can call in @/A/minotaurs).  You can safely melee from
on top of the E.  Digging will dig a semi-permanent E.

If you don't have reflection, lightning (from wands or dragon breath
especially) can blow up your wands (so I'd keep a valuable /death in
the bag to protect it), but you're generally better off having at
least one perma-E in main inv and risking losing it (until you see
something with a /lightning or a blue dragon or whatever).  Electric
eels are always a threat to rings/wands but are easy to avoid.

> I have never met a Vampire before, and am unsure how powerful it is.
